    "result_text": "AcceptanceTest is the only test class (the other two files are a base and a helper). The full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed city-to-region table, exposed as a read-only field on the owner response.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`util/CityRegions.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, single-responsibility class owning the fixed city-to-region table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`) with `localityOf(city)` returning the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"`. The table lives in one place rather than being scattered.\n\n2. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `locality` mapping alongside the existing derived fields (`displayName`, `membershipTier`, etc.), delegating to `CityRegions.localityOf(owner.getCity())`. This follows the established pattern where read-only, computed response fields are derived in the mapper rather than stored on the entity.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `locality` read-only property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\nNo OfficeFloor pipeline changes were needed: `locality` is a pure derivation of an existing field, so it belongs in the DTO mapping used by the existing `RespondWithOwner` / `RespondWithOwnerCreated` responders, not as a new pipeline step.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` for Sydney, `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) pass, and the full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 2/2 tests, 0 failures).",
